abstract: >-
  QSOL UFF v5.1.0 retains the galaxy-dynamics, compact-object, UFF-SLFA,
  Sheridan Crucible, provenance, and independent-assessment systems from
  v5.0.0 while adding a deliberately small defense-in-depth assurance layer.
  A QEC-inspired fail-closed boundary gate enforces strict canonical evidence
  bundles and requires fresh numerical replay for admission. A
  SPECTRAL-inspired witness freezes pre-observation contract, catalogue, and
  support-grid identities and binds them to the contract actually replayed.
  A statistical-mechanics guardrail separates replay verification from future
  null-ensemble calibration, and a SONIFICATION-inspired receiver-neutral event
  stream exposes read-only forensic telemetry. These mechanisms strengthen
  computational assurance; they do not establish physical ontology, historical
  analyst blindness, catalogue independence, null-model adequacy, or causal
  truth.
